{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adevtext1x10000000000000000","parentId":"adevcard1000000000000000000","rootId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"text","title":"## How this works\n\n1. Set up a folder for the agent to work in — the app asks for one when the board is set up.\n2. Make a card and describe the task in it the way you would explain it to a person: what is needed, and how to tell it is done.\n3. Put an agent in the card’s «Assignee» field and drag the card into the «In progress» column: the move is what starts the agent. If it has a question, the question appears on the card.\n4. When it finishes, the agent moves the card on itself, into the column whose name says what happened. What it made is in the folder.\n\nThis card can be deleted — it starts nothing.\n\nThe folder for this board is a repository: the agent works in a copy, leaves a branch behind and does not touch your own working copy.","fields":{},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adevcard2000000000000000000","parentId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","rootId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"card","title":"Update the dependencies","fields":{"contentOrder":["adevtext2x10000000000000000"],"icon":"📦","isTemplate":false,"properties":{"a972dc7a-5f4c-45d2-8044-8c28c69717f1":"ayz81h9f3dwp7rzzbdebesc7ute","d3d682bf-e074-49d9-8df5-7320921c2d23":"87f59784-b859-4c24-8ebe-17c766e081dd"}},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adevtext2x10000000000000000","parentId":"adevcard2000000000000000000","rootId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"text","title":"## What is needed\nUpdate the dependencies to their current versions and fix whatever that breaks.\n\nMajor versions one at a time, with a commit of its own for each: that way it is clear what exactly moved.\n\n## How to tell it is done\nThe project builds, the tests pass, the app starts. At the end — what was updated and what had to be fixed.","fields":{},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adevcard3000000000000000000","parentId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","rootId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"card","title":"Get to the bottom of a failing test","fields":{"contentOrder":["adevtext3x10000000000000000"],"icon":"🎲","isTemplate":false,"properties":{"a972dc7a-5f4c-45d2-8044-8c28c69717f1":"ayz81h9f3dwp7rzzbdebesc7ute","d3d682bf-e074-49d9-8df5-7320921c2d23":"d3bfb50f-f569-4bad-8a3a-dd15c3f60101"}},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
{"type":"block","data":{"id":"adevtext3x10000000000000000","parentId":"adevcard3000000000000000000","rootId":"buz8dcekwdibq3eqjq74w613rxy","createdBy":"system","modifiedBy":"system","schema":1,"type":"text","title":"## What is needed\nThe test fails now and then — find the cause and fix it.\n\nFirst get it to fail every time (run it repeatedly, look for shared state and timing), and only then fix it. Muting the test is not a fix.\n\n## How to tell it is done\nA hundred runs in a row are green, and the reason it was failing has been stated.","fields":{},"createAt":1785888000000,"updateAt":1785888000000,"deleteAt":0}}
